    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d380">

                <pb facs="0770" n="704" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v02/pg704"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2625</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-11-04">November 4, 1941</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Before leaving for Hong Kong via Canton by Japanese plane early tomorrow morning,
                    Mr. Kurusu<anchor n="38a" xml:id="d380-f1"/> called to see me this evening. He
                    said that he has been studying the official papers in connection with his
                    mission to the United States ever since he had been told, only yesterday, of the
                    Foreign Minister’s desire that he proceed to Washington. Mr. Kurusu informed me
                    that he is going simply to help the Japanese Ambassador in the present difficult
                    situation by bringing a fresh point of view and in order that no possible stone
                    be left <pb facs="0771" n="705" xml:id="pg705"/> unturned in the endeavor to
                    bring to a successful conclusion the conversations being conducted between the
                    Japanese and American Governments.</p>
                <p>Mr. Kurusu said that he was taking with him as his secretary Mr. Shiroji Yuki
                    who, as Chief of the First Section of the American Bureau of the Foreign Office,
                    has been most helpful to the Embassy and is familiar with the development of the
                    conversations in Washington.</p>
                <closer><signed>J[<hi rendition="#small-caps">oseph</hi>] C. G[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">rew</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d380-f1" n="38a" xml:id="d380-f1-content">
                <p>Saburo Kurusu, former Japanese Ambassador in Germany.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
